.TH JSON_NEWNODE 3 "JSON Utility" "LIBJSON" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
json_newnode - Create a new JSON node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/json/json.h>
.PP
.B jsonval* json_newnode(jsontype type);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B json_newnode
function creates a new JSON node with the specified
.IR type .
The function returns a pointer to the new JSON node, or NULL if memory allocation fails.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I type
The type of the new JSON node.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns a pointer to the new JSON node, or NULL if memory allocation fails.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the
.B json_newnode
function:
.PP
.B #include <lib/json/json.h>
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.B int main() {
.B \tjsonval* node = json_newnode(JSON_OBJECT);
.B \tif (node) {
.B \t\tprintf("Node created\n");
.B \t\tjson_free(node);
.B \t}
.B \treturn 0;
.B }
.SH SEE ALSO
.B json_init,
.B json_free